  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DRG: Civil Society and Media Strengthening - Stronger Together and Advancing in New Directions (CSM-STAND)/LAC, Asia and E&amp;E</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(USAID Bureau for Development, Democracy, and Innovation (D):  .The purpose of CSM-STAND is to identify and foster effective approaches to strengthen civic engagement and independent media and increase the use of these approaches by USAID Missions, civil society, and independent media in support of DRG and other development results. CSM-STAND strengthens civil society and media capacities to represent citizen interests; defend institutions of democracy; hold governments and private sector actors accountable through advocacy, oversight, and outreach; prevent conflict; and promote resilience. FY 2022 funds will build on past efforts to generate learning materials and practical tools to improve Missions&apos; civil society, media, labor, and youth related activity design and management. CSM-STAND activities will produce technical materials and facilitate engagement of relevant thinkers and practitioners as a way to share information and promote regional and cross-Mission learning. CSM-STAND will support technical resources that advance the integration of pluralist approaches into the design and implementation of programming, the development of an online learning platform, and implementation of a global learning agenda that will promote the accumulation of evidence, peer learning, and trans-regional collaboration across civil society and media sectors. The learning agenda will focus on improving interventions that advance the safety and wellbeing of journalists, activists and organizations; strengthen networks, collaboration and collective action across borders; and increase integrity of information and trustworthiness of media and civic institutions. Associate Awards under CSM-STAND will continue to prioritize the protection of fundamental socio-political rights and freedoms, as part of promoting democratic resilience, transparent, citizen-responsive governance and democratic norms and institutions; and working with local actors to increase civic and media capacities as a w</narrative>
  </description>
